\DOC DISCARD_MATCHING_ASSUMPTIONS

\TYPE {DISCARD_MATCHING_ASSUMPTIONS : term list -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
{DISCARD_MATCHING_ASSUMPTIONS pats} removes from the assumption list every
assumption matching any of the given term patterns, leaving the conclusion
unchanged.

\DESCRIBE
The argument {pats : term list} is a list of patterns whose free variables act
as wildcards, instantiable when matched against an assumption; any assumption
matching at least one pattern is discarded.
{
          A ?- t
     ==================  DISCARD_MATCHING_ASSUMPTIONS pats
          A' ?- t
}
\noindent where {A'} is {A} minus the assumptions matching {pats}, the
surviving assumptions keeping their original relative order (so later
assumptions are renumbered). A single call may remove any number of
assumptions: several matches of one pattern, matches of different patterns, or
none at all, in which case the goal is returned unchanged.

\COMMENTS
The observed traces show only this one kind of outcome, always a single
resulting goal with an unchanged conclusion.

\ENDDOC
